      "content": "hey i was looking at some high res satellite imagery of dc on google maps and noticed something weird about the way the street grids and the memorial layouts are positioned. if u look at the geometry of the main axes it almost looks like a massive fractal antenna or a resonant circuit. do u think it's possible the urban layout was actually designed with specific electromagnetic properties in mind?",
